public static Class<?>[] resolveArguments(Type genericType, Class<?> targetType) {
    if (!(genericType instanceof ParameterizedType)) {
        return null;
    }

    ParameterizedType parameterizedType = (ParameterizedType) genericType;
    Type[] actualTypeArguments = parameterizedType.getActualTypeArguments();
    Class<?>[] resolvedArguments = new Class<?>[actualTypeArguments.length];

    for (int i = 0; i < actualTypeArguments.length; i++) {
        Type type = actualTypeArguments[i];
        if (type instanceof Class) {
            resolvedArguments[i] = (Class<?>) type;
        } else if (type instanceof TypeVariable) {
            // Attempt to resolve type variable against the target type
            Type resolvedType = resolveTypeVariable(targetType, (TypeVariable<?>) type);
            if (resolvedType instanceof Class) {
                resolvedArguments[i] = (Class<?>) resolvedType;
            } else {
                return null; // Unable to resolve type variable
            }
        } else {
            return null; // Unsupported type
        }
    }

    return resolvedArguments;
}

private static Type resolveTypeVariable(Class<?> targetType, TypeVariable<?> typeVariable) {
    Class<?> currentType = targetType;
    while (currentType != null && !Object.class.equals(currentType)) {
        Type genericSuperclass = currentType.getGenericSuperclass();
        if (genericSuperclass instanceof ParameterizedType) {
            ParameterizedType parameterizedType = (ParameterizedType) genericSuperclass;
            Type[] actualTypeArguments = parameterizedType.getActualTypeArguments();
            TypeVariable<?>[] typeParameters = currentType.getSuperclass().getTypeParameters();
            for (int i = 0; i < typeParameters.length; i++) {
                if (typeVariable.equals(typeParameters[i])) {
                    return actualTypeArguments[i];
                }
            }
        }
        currentType = currentType.getSuperclass();
    }
    return null; // Unable to resolve type variable
}
```

This code attempts to resolve the generic type arguments for a given `genericType` using the type variable information for the `targetType`. It includes a helper method `resolveTypeVariable` to resolve type variables against the type hierarchy of `targetType`. If the `genericType` is not parameterized or if the arguments cannot be resolved, the method returns `null`.

